{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}]},{"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class for each "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property. A view reading "},{"code":"store.items","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading","level":2,"anchor":"Effect-Threading"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Design Principles","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Effect","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SwiduxObservable","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"}}}